1
00:00:38,621 --> 00:00:40,832
'Pacino Espresso'

2
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,170
Even a taxi driver
who regularly picks up the same passengers

3
00:00:45,253 --> 00:00:46,671
has a regular place.

4
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:51,050
This place sells
nothing but espresso.

5
00:01:04,314 --> 00:01:05,356
I can never drink

6
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:07,192
espresso straight.

7
00:01:07,275 --> 00:01:08,651
It's much too bitter.

8
00:01:09,861 --> 00:01:11,821
When I add the ice
water I bring from home,

9
00:01:11,905 --> 00:01:13,990
I get it at the low price of an espresso

10
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:17,160
but can enjoy a delicious iced Americano.

11
00:01:19,287 --> 00:01:22,082
Since my job requires me to sit
all day long,

12
00:01:22,165 --> 00:01:23,833
a café like this, where you stand,

13
00:01:23,917 --> 00:01:26,920
helps me maintain my leg strength.

14
00:01:29,672 --> 00:01:31,674
The barista here, Mr. Ma Dae-il,

15
00:01:31,758 --> 00:01:33,802
is also one of my regular passengers.

16
00:01:58,368 --> 00:02:00,662
What brings you to Pohang?

17
00:02:01,246 --> 00:02:02,872
I'm going to get my hair done.

18
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:06,793
Mr. Ma Dae-il travels all the way
to Pohang to get his hair done.

19
00:02:07,585 --> 00:02:09,796
It's just as hard to understand

20
00:02:09,879 --> 00:02:11,464
as drinking espresso.

21
00:02:35,321 --> 00:02:38,783
If you're going all the way to Pohang
for a haircut,

22
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:40,660
it must be a very famous salon.

23
00:02:42,912 --> 00:02:44,789
There's a personal reason.

24
00:02:49,627 --> 00:02:52,297
I have four hair whorls,

25
00:02:56,175 --> 00:02:58,136
and my head is shaped unusually.

26
00:02:59,637 --> 00:03:01,055
At beauty school,

27
00:03:01,139 --> 00:03:03,892
they never taught them how
to handle hair like this.

28
00:03:06,769 --> 00:03:08,813
I'm so sorry.

29
00:03:10,106 --> 00:03:11,524
Oh, no.
It's all right.

30
00:03:11,608 --> 00:03:12,525
Our salon manager

31
00:03:12,609 --> 00:03:15,236
said not to charge you
for the service.

32
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:18,489
Yes.

33
00:03:20,783 --> 00:03:21,701
All my life,

34
00:03:21,784 --> 00:03:24,287
no one has ever done my hair properly.

35
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:29,334
I've gone from salon to salon,

36
00:03:29,417 --> 00:03:31,169
never settling anywhere.

37
00:03:31,753 --> 00:03:35,381
I think you're the first person
I've heard of with four hair whorls.

38
00:03:36,507 --> 00:03:38,134
But then I met her.

39
00:03:45,016 --> 00:03:48,561
Typhoons rising from the equator

40
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:51,439
and typhoons approaching
from the North Pacific—

41
00:03:52,482 --> 00:03:54,442
with storms like these,

42
00:03:54,525 --> 00:03:56,236
you must have suffered quite a
bit of damage over the years.

43
00:04:02,659 --> 00:04:05,119
There's hardly any flat ground,
and the terrain is very uneven,

44
00:04:05,203 --> 00:04:08,957
so even using clippers to cut it short
looks a little dangerous.

45
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:12,043
Still, judging by how lush the forest is,

46
00:04:12,126 --> 00:04:14,003
you don't have to worry about hair loss.

47
00:04:42,782 --> 00:04:44,242
You must be sleepy.

48
00:04:46,119 --> 00:04:46,953
Yes.

49
00:04:47,036 --> 00:04:49,622
When someone touches my hair,
I get so sleepy.

50
00:04:50,456 --> 00:04:51,666
Sleep comfortably.

51
00:04:51,749 --> 00:04:54,669
Your hair is pretty challenging,
so this may take a while.

52
00:05:15,023 --> 00:05:16,232
Sir?

53
00:05:17,525 --> 00:05:18,359
Sir?

54
00:05:34,792 --> 00:05:37,545
It felt like I'd found
a companion for life.

55
00:05:44,761 --> 00:05:45,678
What?

56
00:05:46,262 --> 00:05:47,430
When did the music stop?

57
00:05:48,056 --> 00:05:49,474
Excuse me, Sir.

58
00:05:49,557 --> 00:05:50,391
Yes?

59
00:06:00,985 --> 00:06:06,365
♪ When I take a quiet walk at night ♪

60
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:11,621
♪ There's a face I always think of ♪

61
00:06:11,704 --> 00:06:14,457
Ms. Yoo-jin,
this song again?

62
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:15,583
What's wrong with this song?

63
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:17,543
It's so sad.

64
00:06:18,127 --> 00:06:21,881
That's because Ms. Clara
had a painful love.

65
00:06:22,465 --> 00:06:23,299
Hey.

66
00:06:23,382 --> 00:06:24,550
I'm all healed now, you know?

67
00:06:28,471 --> 00:06:30,348
You must listen to this song a lot.

68
00:06:31,099 --> 00:06:32,517
The lyrics are sad,

69
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:35,770
but listening to it
always cheers me up.

70
00:06:35,853 --> 00:06:38,022
Is that weird?

71
00:06:38,106 --> 00:06:42,360
No. When I hear upbeat songs,
my stomach starts hurting for no reason.

72
00:06:44,278 --> 00:06:47,031
I think you and I
are on the same wavelength.

73
00:06:48,658 --> 00:06:50,409
Yes, I think so too.

74
00:06:50,493 --> 00:06:54,622
♪ You fade away like a picture ♪

75
00:06:54,705 --> 00:06:56,958
♪ I miss you so ♪

76
00:06:57,041 --> 00:07:02,255
♪ Thinking of that person again today ♪

77
00:07:02,338 --> 00:07:05,424
♪ I take a walk ♪

78
00:07:08,386 --> 00:07:10,221
This song is really good.

79
00:07:11,305 --> 00:07:13,391
It's called 'A Walk.'

80
00:07:13,474 --> 00:07:16,602
This song reminds me
of a friend, too.

81
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:17,937
His name was Doo-shik.

82
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:21,816
He always waited for me
to finish work,

83
00:07:21,899 --> 00:07:24,902
and we'd take a walk
near home every day.

84
00:07:29,282 --> 00:07:32,743
Your boyfriend must
have been a freelancer.

85
00:07:32,827 --> 00:07:35,496
Well, you could call him male,

86
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:37,206
but we usually say 'a male.'

87
00:07:39,041 --> 00:07:40,501
He was my dog.

88
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:46,466
Our Doo-shik is on the other side
of the Rainbow Bridge now.

89
00:07:46,549 --> 00:07:50,261
He must be taking walks
every day there, too.

90
00:07:50,344 --> 00:07:54,307
So Doo-shik was your dog's name.

91
00:07:54,390 --> 00:07:57,935
I called him Doo-shik
because he had a big head and ate a lot.

92
00:07:59,395 --> 00:08:02,982
He'd jump right up and smile
just at the word 'walk.'

93
00:08:03,065 --> 00:08:06,611
I miss seeing our Doo-shik's face.

94
00:08:07,403 --> 00:08:09,947
♪ Your eyes ♪

95
00:08:10,031 --> 00:08:11,699
♪ Your heart ♪

96
00:08:11,782 --> 00:08:18,206
♪ Giving love
without asking for anything ♪

97
00:08:18,289 --> 00:08:24,587
♪ I find myself missing her ♪

98
00:08:24,670 --> 00:08:27,548
♪ That face I long for ♪

99
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:32,595
♪ It fades like a picture
painted on water ♪

100
00:08:32,678 --> 00:08:34,805
Every three weeks, without fail,

101
00:08:34,889 --> 00:08:37,683
I had my hair cut by Yujin.

102
00:08:39,185 --> 00:08:41,354
How many people do we regularly meet

103
00:08:41,437 --> 00:08:43,272
every three weeks?

104
00:08:44,565 --> 00:08:46,734
I think Yujin was the only one for me.

105
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:51,364
So you had really settled
in at Milano Hair?

106
00:08:53,699 --> 00:08:55,034
Well, I...

107
00:08:55,117 --> 00:08:58,204
I had, until I ruined everything.

108
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:09,590
Please lower your head a little.

109
00:09:11,551 --> 00:09:13,302
A little more, please.

110
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:28,359
Please don't move your head.

111
00:09:28,442 --> 00:09:29,694
I'm sorry.

112
00:09:41,205 --> 00:09:43,165
I said, please don't move your head.

113
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:44,834
Yes.

114
00:10:04,562 --> 00:10:05,396
How is it?

115
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:08,399
I like it. Yujin, I really like you.

116
00:10:10,318 --> 00:10:11,193
What?

117
00:10:12,111 --> 00:10:13,821
I really like you, Yujin.

118
00:10:24,832 --> 00:10:25,666
Sir.

119
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:29,754
Sir.

120
00:10:41,223 --> 00:10:43,142
It was a confession in my dream,

121
00:10:44,769 --> 00:10:47,438
but I ended up saying
it out loud in my sleep.

122
00:10:48,689 --> 00:10:50,775
I'll shampoo your hair. This way.

123
00:10:55,029 --> 00:10:56,989
Could I shampoo it at home?

124
00:10:57,698 --> 00:10:58,532
What?

125
00:11:04,246 --> 00:11:05,081
Goodbye...

126
00:11:06,666 --> 00:11:08,250
Sir, you need to take your card.

127
00:11:12,588 --> 00:11:13,881
I'm sorry, but...

128
00:11:14,715 --> 00:11:17,635
Could you tell me the whole
story without stopping?

129
00:11:17,718 --> 00:11:19,595
I'm so curious, I feel like I'm
going to get motion sickness.

130
00:11:22,139 --> 00:11:23,265
Yes.

131
00:11:23,349 --> 00:11:26,143
Three weeks later,
I went back to Milano Hair.

132
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:29,230
It was my routine.

133
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:35,111
- What?
- Yujin left for personal reasons.

134
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:36,904
She quit last month.

135
00:11:39,824 --> 00:11:42,410
Then could you at least give
me Yujin's contact information?

136
00:11:43,702 --> 00:11:45,204
Due to our company policy,

137
00:11:45,287 --> 00:11:47,540
we can't give out her personal
contact information...

138
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:50,000
Because of me,

139
00:11:50,084 --> 00:11:52,294
I think Yujin left the salon.

140
00:11:53,838 --> 00:11:55,131
At her workplace, in front of everyone,

141
00:11:55,214 --> 00:11:57,550
it was essentially a public confession.

142
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:01,512
I had lost the one stylist

143
00:12:01,595 --> 00:12:03,139
who could truly manage my hair.

144
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:07,893
I was devastated.

145
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:12,773
I tried a few hair salons,

146
00:12:12,857 --> 00:12:15,943
but my hair started sticking out
all over the place again.

147
00:12:17,194 --> 00:12:19,071
I had no choice but to wear a hat.

148
00:12:21,198 --> 00:12:22,366
After that,

149
00:12:23,284 --> 00:12:26,036
I haven't had my hair cut
once since then.

150
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:28,307
But

151
00:13:28,390 --> 00:13:31,268
How did you find out
that Ms. Yujin was in Pohang?

152
00:13:32,895 --> 00:13:35,231
I was watching 'My Hometown at 6:30,'

153
00:13:35,314 --> 00:13:37,525
and Ms. Yujin appeared
on the Pohang episode.

154
00:13:37,608 --> 00:13:38,692
The caption said,

155
00:13:39,401 --> 00:13:40,819
'Pohang's Steelworks
Scissorhands, ' or something?

156
00:13:42,112 --> 00:13:45,199
That name alone
makes me trust you.

157
00:14:06,262 --> 00:14:07,596
We've arrived.

158
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:09,348
Yes.

159
00:14:24,697 --> 00:14:25,990
Welcome.

160
00:14:37,459 --> 00:14:39,253
Mr. Ma Dae-il?

161
00:14:40,629 --> 00:14:42,464
Yes, it's been a while.

162
00:14:53,517 --> 00:14:55,519
Thank you.

163
00:14:55,603 --> 00:14:56,562
What did you say?

164
00:14:57,563 --> 00:14:59,440
Hey, open that lid for me.

165
00:15:00,232 --> 00:15:02,985
My hands are busy.

166
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:04,737
I can't open the lid.

167
00:15:05,529 --> 00:15:07,156
Yes, yes.

168
00:15:07,239 --> 00:15:08,073
Yeah.

169
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:13,078
Here.

170
00:15:16,665 --> 00:15:18,584
I didn't think you'd
recognize me right away.

171
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:22,004
How could I forget someone
with four cowlicks?

172
00:15:22,713 --> 00:15:23,714
That's right.

173
00:15:24,882 --> 00:15:27,009
Do you have a style in mind?

174
00:15:28,135 --> 00:15:29,511
I'd like to leave it to Ms. Yujin.

175
00:15:30,220 --> 00:15:32,389
Yujin was

176
00:15:32,473 --> 00:15:34,433
an alias I used at my old salon.

177
00:15:34,516 --> 00:15:36,894
My name is Heon-ju. Lee Heon-ju.

178
00:15:38,687 --> 00:15:40,564
Heon-ju, then.

179
00:15:41,690 --> 00:15:43,484
Look over here.
Take a look at this.

180
00:15:43,567 --> 00:15:45,986
Ma'am, why are you taking that off?
You need to leave it on a little longer.

181
00:15:46,070 --> 00:15:48,739
If you roll it this loosely,

182
00:15:48,822 --> 00:15:51,325
what if the perm comes out too quickly?

183
00:15:51,408 --> 00:15:54,536
Don't you trust my skills?

184
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:55,913
Someone came all the way here

185
00:15:55,996 --> 00:15:58,999
from Seoul to get their hair cut by me.

186
00:15:59,083 --> 00:16:00,084
If it comes out right away,

187
00:16:00,167 --> 00:16:02,711
I'll do it again for free.

188
00:16:02,795 --> 00:16:03,921
Put that back on.

189
00:16:04,922 --> 00:16:06,382
Yes, go ahead and use it.
I...

190
00:16:06,465 --> 00:16:08,634
What is it?

191
00:16:09,426 --> 00:16:10,803
I'm a taxi driver.

192
00:16:12,429 --> 00:16:13,263
Here, here.

193
00:16:14,014 --> 00:16:15,683
-
-

194
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:19,603
The atmosphere is very different
from the old salon, isn't it?

195
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:23,774
Ms. Heon-ju.

196
00:16:23,857 --> 00:16:24,900
Yes.

197
00:16:25,901 --> 00:16:27,152
I'm sorry about that day.

198
00:16:31,031 --> 00:16:32,950
The last day I saw you,

199
00:16:33,575 --> 00:16:35,452
because of what I said in my sleep,

200
00:16:35,536 --> 00:16:37,579
I thought you'd left
the salon because of it.

201
00:16:38,706 --> 00:16:40,374
I've always felt sorry.

202
00:16:50,509 --> 00:16:52,386
Mr. Ma Dae-il,

203
00:16:52,469 --> 00:16:55,305
are you referring to the day
you snored so loudly in your sleep?

204
00:17:14,199 --> 00:17:16,285
Aren't you going to damage
your nose if you keep that up?

205
00:17:19,455 --> 00:17:21,206
Everyone, stop staring over here

206
00:17:21,290 --> 00:17:23,375
and don't make it too
obvious to the customer.

207
00:17:24,084 --> 00:17:24,918
Ms. Clara,

208
00:17:25,002 --> 00:17:27,212
could you turn up the music in the salon?

209
00:17:28,505 --> 00:17:29,923
Was music playing?

210
00:17:41,018 --> 00:17:46,899
♪ I wanted us to be
the happiest couple in the world ♪

211
00:17:47,691 --> 00:17:48,525
♪ The happiest in the world... ♪

212
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:54,114
I told everyone not to make it obvious,

213
00:17:54,198 --> 00:17:56,241
but you left right away
without even getting a shampoo,

214
00:17:56,325 --> 00:17:58,118
so I thought you'd been hurt.

215
00:17:58,786 --> 00:18:01,205
Then why did you quit
the hair salon?

216
00:18:02,331 --> 00:18:05,334
My mother's eyesight
became very poor.

217
00:18:05,417 --> 00:18:07,586
So poor that she could
no longer hold scissors.

218
00:18:07,669 --> 00:18:10,339
This was my mother's salon.

219
00:18:11,048 --> 00:18:12,966
It was a salon she ran under my name,

220
00:18:13,050 --> 00:18:14,510
so I decided to carry it on.

221
00:18:51,421 --> 00:18:53,090
I missed you.

222
00:18:57,427 --> 00:18:59,596
That guy

223
00:19:00,305 --> 00:19:03,225
kept saying he wanted to see
the ocean on the way here.

224
00:19:23,328 --> 00:19:24,496
All done.

225
00:19:37,551 --> 00:19:40,721
Mr. Dae-il, this hairstyle
really suits you.

226
00:19:40,804 --> 00:19:43,807
It looks like you've
made it your own style.

227
00:19:43,891 --> 00:19:47,060
I only trimmed the ends
and adjusted the volume.

228
00:19:47,144 --> 00:19:49,062
Making your hair heavy

229
00:19:49,146 --> 00:19:51,315
keeps your cowlick from doing its job.

230
00:19:52,232 --> 00:19:54,318
I think, Mr. Dae-il,

231
00:19:54,401 --> 00:19:56,862
you seemed to like this style.

232
00:19:58,530 --> 00:20:00,657
You still know without me
having to say anything.

233
00:20:24,056 --> 00:20:24,973
But, seriously.

234
00:20:25,849 --> 00:20:28,310
You fall asleep as soon
as she touched your hair.

235
00:20:29,478 --> 00:20:32,731
Well, tonight, I didn't fall asleep
for even a second.

236
00:20:35,901 --> 00:20:37,277
Oh, then...

237
00:20:37,361 --> 00:20:40,322
So when you said you missed her,
you weren't talking in your sleep?

238
00:20:41,323 --> 00:20:42,866
No.

239
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:43,951
Like Ms. Heon-ju said,

240
00:20:44,034 --> 00:20:45,994
I actually like my hair
just the way it is now.

241
00:20:46,995 --> 00:20:48,830
I just wanted to see her.

242
00:20:49,915 --> 00:20:52,209
Oh, well, then...
Should I turn the car around?

243
00:20:52,292 --> 00:20:53,168
No, no.

244
00:20:53,877 --> 00:20:55,712
Funny enough, I like bitter things.

245
00:20:56,672 --> 00:20:58,757
Sweet things just aren't
my style, I guess.

246
00:21:10,394 --> 00:21:11,478
Shall we listen to a song?

247
00:21:26,994 --> 00:21:32,666
♪ On a quiet nighttime stroll ♪

248
00:21:32,749 --> 00:21:38,380
♪ A face comes to mind, without fail ♪

249
00:21:38,463 --> 00:21:42,009
♪ Shimmering ♪

250
00:21:42,092 --> 00:21:46,972
♪ I gather stars to sketch ♪

251
00:21:47,055 --> 00:21:49,808
♪ Someone like that ♪

252
00:21:49,891 --> 00:21:55,647
♪ Filling the narrow lane with fragrance ♪

253
00:21:55,731 --> 00:22:01,570
♪ Azaleas tinted by the streetlamps ♪

254
00:22:01,653 --> 00:22:04,865
♪ This fragrance ♪

255
00:22:04,948 --> 00:22:09,786
♪ If only I could smell it with her ♪

256
00:22:09,870 --> 00:22:12,247
♪ How lovely that would be ♪

257
00:22:12,331 --> 00:22:17,627
♪ I miss that beloved face ♪

258
00:22:17,711 --> 00:22:20,172
♪ Like a picture painted in water ♪

259
00:22:20,255 --> 00:22:23,717
♪ It fades away ♪

260
00:22:23,800 --> 00:22:26,219
♪ Oh, how I miss her ♪

261
00:22:26,303 --> 00:22:31,892
♪ To remember her again today ♪

262
00:22:31,975 --> 00:22:35,062
♪ I take a walk ♪

263
00:22:47,365 --> 00:22:52,662
♪ The cold air wraps around me ♪

264
00:22:52,746 --> 00:22:58,752
♪ Those days come vividly to mind ♪

265
00:22:58,835 --> 00:23:01,963
♪ Those precious ♪

266
